Object.assign(messages.en,{aboutModel:'About this model',modelLimits:'An educational approximation for play and experiments. This is not an agronomy forecast or a recommendation for real farming decisions.',modelUnits:'One bed represents 1 m². 1 mm of water over that bed equals 1 litre. Each soil reservoir holds up to 50 mm; all water-balance terms use the same units.',modelBalance:'Each game hour: rain + irrigation enter the soil; crop water use, evaporation and drainage leave it. Dry or waterlogged soil slows growth and gently reduces quality. Appropriate care can recover quality.',modelAssumptions:'Weather is a seeded game pattern, not a local forecast. Crop durations, yields, prices and energy costs are fictional balance values. Nutrients, soil types, pests and real climate are simplified or omitted. The clock pauses in inactive tabs; no offline damage is applied.'});
